{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Bind one handler per event and let the SDK compose them into the single","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handler ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/reactorServe(config:transport:handler:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" takes.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ReactorRouter"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"§22.10’s handler is ONE function from an event to one answer, which is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"right shape for the wire and the wrong shape for the code. A reactor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"registered for three events opens with a ","type":"text"},{"code":"switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"code":"event.event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and that","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"switch is where two defects live. The first is cheap: a misspelled event name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binds nothing and is discovered as an event that never fires. The second is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not — it is the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"default:"},{"text":" arm that returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".allow"},{"text":" on behalf of code that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never ran, which is §22.10 rule 2’s defect relocated into user code where the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rule does not reach it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A BUILDER RATHER THAN AN ATTRIBUTE"}]},{"text":", and §22.14 records why: a Swift","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reactor handler is an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"text":" closure, and collecting ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"text":" members by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reflection costs a runtime dependency an SDK should not add to hand out an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute. A builder type-checks the closure against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(ReactorEvent) async throws -> ReactorAnswer"},{"text":" at compile time, which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stricter than what the reflection would have bought. Kotlin made the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trade for the same reason.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"PURE SUGAR."}]},{"type":"text","text":" It opens no connection, consumes no queue, verifies no event,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"signs no reply and interprets no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timeout_ms"},{"type":"text","text":"; its output is exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"handler the runtime accepts (rule 1)."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/reactorrouter"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ReactorRouter","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ReactorRouter","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ReactorRouter","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13